# conf/oss-scan.rules — the ONE table of what an internal name or address looks
# like in this repo (issue #3571, EPIC #3569 共同约定 1). Every reader reads
# THIS file, never a copy of a pattern: bin/oss-scan.sh (the inventory, C1),
# the commit gate (C2), the config / placeholder acceptance (C7 / C8), the
# fleet-infra plugin check (C16 / C17).
#
# One rule per line: <rule-id><TAB><ERE><TAB><说明>. The ERE goes to
# `git grep -E` and to awk as written, so it must mean the same to both:
# no \b \d \s \w (spell a boundary out: (^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])), no {m,n}, no (?i)
# — case goes in brackets. A rule id never changes meaning (C2 counts by it).
#
# `#@keep<TAB><text>` — a match whose text (boundary characters trimmed) is
# exactly <text> is not a hit: the repo's own name and the shared placeholder
# words below are what new text is SUPPOSED to say. Where a hit may stay is
# conf/oss-scan.allow (path-glob · rule · reason), never a pattern here.
#
# Shared placeholders for new text (EPIC #3569 共同约定 1): mac-a mac-b linux-a ·
# hub.example.com · relay.example.com · alice bob · example.ts.net.

tailnet	tail435588	our tailscale tailnet's name
ts-net	[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9.-]*\.ts\.net	a tailscale MagicDNS name (a machine on a tailnet)
corp-domain	24haowan|24hw\.cn	our company's domains, image namespace and monorepo name
cloud	aliyuncs\.com|cn-shenzhen|1720148580188583|cff10a18030a74894a0bbc765e21779ef	our cloud: Alibaba registry, region, account id, ACK cluster id
machine	(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_-])(macmini|mini2|fleet-linux-0|m4|m5)([^A-Za-z0-9_-]|$)	our machines' names and their aliases (mini2=m4, macmini=m5)
user-home	/(Users|home)/(verky|verkyyi|verk|victor|arvin|24haowan)([^A-Za-z0-9_.-]|$)	a real login's home directory
person	(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])([Vv]erky|[Vv]erk|[Vv]ictor|[Aa]rvin)([^A-Za-z0-9_]|$)	a real person's name or login
gh-owner	verkyyi(/[A-Za-z0-9_-]+)?	the owner's GitHub handle (the repo's own name is kept below)
private-ipv4	(^|[^0-9.])(10\.[0-9]+|172\.(1[6-9]|2[0-9]|3[01])|192\.168|100\.(6[4-9]|[7-9][0-9]|1[01][0-9]|12[0-7]))\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+	a private / tailnet (CGNAT) IPv4 address

#@keep	verkyyi/claude-fleet
#@keep	example.ts.net
# Standard addresses, never anyone's own (issue #3577): the RFC 1918 / RFC 6598
# block bases a network check spells (10.0.0.0/8 …), and Alibaba Cloud's
# documented instance-metadata address — a guard has to name it to cut it.
#@keep	10.0.0.0
#@keep	172.16.0.0
#@keep	192.168.0.0
#@keep	100.64.0.0
#@keep	100.100.100.200
